From: DKR-R Windows 95 port
Subject: [PATCH] Exclusive sections, and the preemption they reveal

Windows 95 does not implement GetThreadTimes, so every row of the frame budget
is a wall interval, and on one processor a wall interval counts whatever
preempted the thread being timed. Under DKR_TRACE_EXCLUSIVE, a section raises
its thread to time-critical priority. Nothing else in the process can then run
inside it, so its wall interval is its processor time.

The implementation lives here rather than in the game, because this is where the
guest rows become exact. A guest thread cannot execute during another host
thread's exclusive section, so if one is counted as running, the whole section
is preemption. It is charged to that thread in [trace][preempted], and
`ran - preempted` is what the thread used. Sections taken while the idle thread
is parked go to their own bucket, and nested sections count once.

The game's audio microcode, send_dl and update_screen use it through
dkr_exclusive_enter/leave. This patch adds the RDRAM snapshot and each round of
the graphics thread. One run, 100 s, a frame of 120.1 ms:

  [trace][preempted] t1=130911 t3=585801 t4=502444 t5=24779877 us

The scheduler, id 5, was 52.7 s of `ran`: 25.4 s of snapshot, 24.8 s of other
threads' work, and 2.5 s of its own.

